# The GMN\-1 \(GMEOW Model Notation\) surface grammar in W3C EBNF, one production per line

`gmn` · notation grammar · License: `AGPL-3.0-only`

## Grammar source

```ebnf
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Blackcat Informatics® Inc. <paudley@blackcatinformatics.ca>
# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# The GMN-1 (GMEOW Model Notation) surface grammar in W3C EBNF, one production
# per line. This file is a RENDERING of the gmeow:gmnGrammar object in the lang
# module, never its identity: the grammar object carries the normative claims
# (LL(1) prefix decodability via gmeow:gmnDeterminismClass, the sigil-role and
# operator tables). GMN is newline-delimited: every record occupies one line and
# opens with a record-initial sigil, so a reader dispatches on the first token.
# The in-band '@gmn' header pins the dialect coordinates (schema version,
# alias-table reference, and glyph-table version) before any record. Records are sigil-then-braced
# key-value lists; a schema-once tabular batch declares its columns once in an
# '@claims[...]' header and then streams bare rows. Lexical whitespace rules are
# carried by the codec, not by these productions.

gmnDoc ::= header line*
header ::= '@gmn' '{' 'v' ':' integer ',' 'aliases' ':' identifier ',' 'glyphs' ':' integer '}' EOL
